    "no_js": {
      "kind": "no_js",
      "title": "Project knowledge, organized for AI.",
      "command": "git clone https://github.com/aDNA-Network/aDNA.git ~/aDNA && cd ~/aDNA && claude",
      "copyVisible": false,
      "text": "Open standard · MIT\n\nProject knowledge, organized for AI.\n\naDNA (Agentic DNA) is an open standard for organizing a project's files. Three folders and plain Markdown give people and AI agents a shared map.\n\nStart a local workspace with Git and Claude Code.\n\nGet Started\nRead the standard\n\nNew to aDNA? Read the short introduction.\n\n$\ngit clone https://github.com/aDNA-Network/aDNA.git ~/aDNA && cd ~/aDNA && claude\n\nA project you can inspect\naDNA.aDNA/\nThis site's project folder\nCLAUDE.md\nFile\nAgent instructions\nSTATE.md\nFile\nWork in progress\nwhat/\nFolder\nKnowledge and decisions\nhow/\nFolder\nPlans and procedures\nwho/\nFolder\nPeople and roles\nCLAUDE.md excerpt\n\nPhase gates are human gates. Never auto-advance between campaign phases without explicit user approval.\n\nRead the full instruction file\n\nThese are written instructions. The structure does not enforce an agent’s behavior.\n\nNot a product or service — no server, no signup; aDNA itself sends nothing.\n\nThe standard that gives it that shape is open. Your files stay on your machine. Your AI tool has its own data handling.\n\nOpen source on GitHub\nMIT-licensed\nthe standard, versioned and public"
    },
